'''John Nies''' (born February 13, 1967)<ref name="pro">{{cite web|url = https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/N/NiesJo20.htm|publisher = pro-football-reference.com|title = John Nies}}</ref> was a sixth round (154th overall) pick in the [[1990 NFL draft]] out of [[University of Arizona]] to the [[Buffalo Bills]],<ref>{{Cite web |title=1990 NFL Draft Listing |url=https://www.pro-football-reference.com/years/1990/draft.htm |access-date=2023-05-26 |website=Pro-Football-Reference.com |language=en}}</ref> where he played for one year as a [[Punter (American football)|punter]].<ref name="pro"/><ref>{{Cite book|title = NFL 2001 Record and Fact Book|date = March 2001|publisher = Workman Publishing Co, New York, NY|isbn = 0-7611-2480-2|page = [https://archive.org/details/officialnfl2001r0000unse/page/262 262]|url-access = registration|url = https://archive.org/details/officialnfl2001r0000unse/page/262}}</ref><ref name="chi">{{cite web|url=http://www.chiforce7.com/john-nies.php |publisher=Chi Force |title=John Nies |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20090308033007/http://www.chiforce7.com/john-nies.php |archive-date=2009-03-08 }}</ref> Along with his younger brother [[Eric Nies]] (later of [[MTV]]'s ''[[The Real World (TV series)|The Real World]]'' fame),<ref>{{cite web|url = http://www.newyorktails.com/ericnies.htm|title = MTV's Eric Nies and the Real World of Weimaraners, Waistlines and "Reality" TV|first = Diane| last = West}}</ref> John Nies subsequently became a [[Model (person)|fashion model]], actor and host of numerous [[ESPN]] programs.<ref name="chi"/>

John was inspired to start "The Power Center" after a paradigm shifting experience with a Kung Fu Grandmaster and founded The Power Center in early 2000. Finally bringing his passion to life in an intense personal and group fitness training facility.  His trademark training style "East West Chi" is a fusion of [[eastern philosophy|Eastern]] health and wellness philosophies and more contemporary [[Western culture|Western]] training techniques that serve as a model for living a fully integrated life mentally, physically and spiritually.<ref>{{cite web|url = http://www.chiforce7.com/|title = Chi-Force Website}}</ref> John is the owner of The Power Center in [[Red Bank, New Jersey]], a group fitness and personal training facility. At his fitness center and through speaking engagements John Nies focuses on [[prevention of illness]], sport-specific [[Sports training|training program]] for [[sportsperson|athletes]], the cultivation of personal discipline, as well as helping clients overcome [[substance abuse]], [[food addiction]]s, [[insomnia]], [[Clinical depression|depression]], fear and [[anxiety]], low energy levels, and other related complaints related to physical and [[mental health]].<ref name="chi"/>

Nies is a fitness ambassador with Lululemon, a contributor to the newly published book, "Beauty Pearls for Chemo Girls", as an expert on fitness and the power of using your mind and visualization as a tool for healing during chemotherapy for cancer patients.<ref>{{Cite web |url=http://beautypearlsforchemogirls.com/ |title=Home Page|website=beautypearlsforchemogirls.com|access-date=2009-09-06 |archive-date=2010-07-06 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20100706035525/http://beautypearlsforchemogirls.com/ |url-status=dead }}</ref> In addition, he is part of the Hollywood Heroes campaign as a spokesperson for [[Kids Kicking Cancer]], a [[non-profit organization]] dedicated to helping children with [[cancer]] through mind-body training in the [[martial arts]].<ref name="chi"/>
